==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|artificier|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|artificiarius|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone who is skilled in their [[trade]]; an [[artisan]].
#* {{RQ:Authorized Version}}, Genesis 4:22
#*: And Zillah, she also bare Tubal-cain, an instructer of every '''artificer''' in brass and iron: and the sister of Tubal-cain was Naamah.
# An [[inventor]].
# A member of the [[military]] who specializes in manufacturing and repairing [[weapon]] systems.
# A [[trickster]].
# A [[savant]].

====Translations====
* Portuguese: {{t+|pt|artífice}}

